  <h1>Training Journal: Sold Out, and Marathon Plan B</h1>
  <div class="postmeta">November 27, 2026 · Journal</div>

  <article>
    <p>Black Friday update: the Phoenix Marathon has a 15 percent off deal, and
    it is sold out. So the discount I was waiting on to make my decision has
    made the decision for me, at least for that race.</p>

    <h2>The options</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Tucson, December 13.</b> One day after the date I had planned, so
      the training picture is the same as before: 16 days out, longest run of
      this build is 13.1 miles, and my back is still tight.</li>
      <li><b>Vegas, January 10.</b> About six more weeks. That is time to
      get a real long run in, let the back settle, and show up better prepared
      for 26.2.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where my head is</h2>
    <p>Vegas likely makes more sense. This was always meant to be a training
    marathon, and a race that falls apart because I did not give myself the
    long runs is not much of a training run. Six weeks changes what I can
    reasonably aim for. The 4:02 the calculator gave me from the 10 miler was
    the best case on the old timeline. With more miles behind me, it gets
    closer to a real target.</p>
    <p>I will decide by the end of today, and I will report back.</p>

    <p>If you want to see what a finish on that pace looks like, here is the
    <a href="/?d=marathon&amp;u=mi&amp;mode=even&amp;t=4:05:00&amp;eq=half&amp;eqt=1:49:56&amp;profile=1.090">4:05 plan</a>.</p>
  </article>

